WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.131
A transaction groups operations into a logical unit of work.

00:00:04.131 --> 00:00:13.219
Atomicity means the group succeeds as a unit or is not partly applied; consistency, isolation and durability describe other important transaction properties.

00:00:13.219 --> 00:00:17.350
Their exact guarantees depend on the database and chosen settings.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:25.635
Applying only the debit loses money from the represented accounts; applying only the credit creates an inconsistent result.

00:00:25.635 --> 00:00:28.064
Atomic handling avoids this partial-update state.

00:00:28.064 --> 00:00:33.325
A real financial system needs additional validation and controls beyond this teaching example.

00:00:34.325 --> 00:00:37.031
Which property addresses all-or-nothing application?

00:00:37.031 --> 00:00:41.360
Atomicity is the all-or-nothing property of a transaction.
